--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI AlertsList page at web parity: a pure @Observable
state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable
AlertsListDataSource seam whose value types mirror the web `Alert` / `AlertRule`
/ `PinnedItem` / `AlertEvent` / `AlertDetail` 1:1. Production binds the KMP
endpoints behind the seam (GET /alerts, GET /alerts/rules, GET /pinned,
GET /alerts/{id}, POST /alerts/{id}/read, acknowledge/reopen). The list is
control-plane data (no SI units), so the ADR display-boundary conversion is N/A
here (like the sibling Exports / Audit Log pages) — time-ago / counts only.

The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title + subtitle, the header
RangePicker + DataFreshnessAuto refresh + the quiet-hours Badge) and every web
region, each rendering its OWN data state in place rather than gating the surface:

  Overview (web KpiOverviewCard / no-data GlassPanel) — when the window has
    alerts (or a prior period did), a glass card with SIX KPI tiles each carrying
    its prior-period delta (Total / Critical / Warnings / Info / Unread /
    Read-rate), a secondary breakdown line (Active Rules enabled/total · Most
    Common type · Last 7 Days count · "Quiet hours active"), and the danger
    critical callout ("N critical alert needs attention" + "View critical" CTA
    that jumps to the Critical tab). When the window is empty, the web no-data
    GlassPanel with the "No alerts" / alerts.noAlertsInRange EmptyState.

  Alert Trend (7 Days) — the web stacked BarChart of alert counts by severity
    over the trailing 7 days, via the P3 native Swift Charts wrapper TSBarChart
    (stacked critical/warning/info series), with a weekday caption axis + a
    severity legend. Its own empty state when the window has no alerts.

  Alerts by Type — the web donut PieChart via the P3 wrapper TSPieChart, with the
    per-category legend list (color dot + type label + count) the web renders
    beside it. Its own empty state.

  Watching (web pinnedRules GlassPanel) — shown only when alert rules are pinned:
    a "Watching (n)" header and one row per pinned rule (name or "Rule #id"
    fallback) with an enabled/disabled Badge, ordered by pin position.

  Filter bar (web FilterBar + SearchInput + TabNav + ActiveFilterChips) — the
    search field (title/message), the All / Unread / Critical status tabs with
    live counts, and the removable active-filter chips.

  Alert list (web pagedAlerts + AlertCard + pagination) — the paginated alert
    rows (severity-tinted type icon, title + message, unread status dot, time-ago
    / severity / type / acknowledged meta, and the audit-timeline / acknowledge-
    or-reopen / mark-read actions), the "Showing m–n of total" footer + paging,
    and its own EmptyState (no-search / search-miss / fleet-healthy variants).

  Acknowledge dialog (web AcknowledgeAlertDialog) + Audit-timeline sheet (web
    detail Modal + AlertDetailTimeline) — adaptive sheets; the timeline shows the
    loading skeleton / event rail / no-events empty the web detailQuery drives.
    Mutations surface the web toasts ("Alert marked as read", acknowledge success
    + Undo→reopen).

Files (all under apps/apple/Sources/Features/Notifications/, + the test):
  AlertsListModels.swift          — AlertsSeverity (normalize), AlertsAlert,
                                    AlertsRule, AlertsPin, AlertsEvent,
                                    AlertsDetail, AlertsQuietHours (isActive),
                                    AlertsFilter, AlertsRange, AlertsTabCounts,
                                    AlertsFilterChip.
  AlertsListAggregation.swift     — pure web useMemo pipeline: overview counts,
                                    readRate, range/prior windows, byType, the
                                    7-day byDay stacked trend, weekCount,
                                    pinnedRules, tab/search filters, percent/
                                    absolute deltas + AlertsListFormat.
  AlertsListPageModel.swift       — @MainActor @Observable model: phases, derived
                                    list pipeline, mark-read/acknowledge/reopen,
                                    audit-timeline load, filter/range/page state.
  AlertsListPageModel.Sample.swift— SampleAlertsListDataSource + Empty/Failing/
                                    QuietHours preview seams.
  AlertsListPage.swift            — the View: chrome, phase switch, ready
                                    scaffold, single-sheet router, action toast.
  AlertsListPage.Overview.swift   — KPI overview card / no-data panel + KPI tile +
                                    secondary line.
  AlertsListPage.Charts.swift     — TSBarChart trend + TSPieChart by-type + legend.
  AlertsListPage.Sections.swift   — Watching panel + filter bar + status tabs.
  AlertsListPage.List.swift       — alert rows + pagination + list empties +
                                    loading skeleton + type-icon map.
  AlertsListPage.Dialogs.swift    — acknowledge dialog + timeline sheet + toast.
  AlertsListRouteRegistration.swift — registers `.alerts` into the shell registry.
  Tests/Unit/Features/Notifications/AlertsListPageModelTests.swift — 24 unit tests.

Navigation: AppRoute gains `.alerts` (pathSegment "alerts", group .operations,
bell.badge icon, titleKey route.alerts). AppRouteParser maps the web
/notifications/alerts AND the legacy /alerts redirect to `.alerts`.
AlertsListRouteRegistration is threaded into TeslaSyncApp.routeHostRegistry.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
UNITS (ADR-005)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
N/A — alert-log entities carry no SI quantities; the page renders counts, a
read-rate %, and relative time-ago only. No unit conversion is required, exactly
like the sibling Exports / Audit Log control-plane pages.

